From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Palgunov <toxblh@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:01:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 95/99] v8: e2k: grow wasm stacks from the stack of the wasm
 frame

With --wasm-growable-stacks a wasm function whose stack check fails on a
secondary stack calls wasm_grow_stack (WasmHandleStackOverflow), which
decides by the C stack pointer whether it runs on the central stack and
whether the active stack has overflowed.  On e2k C called from a
secondary stack runs on the main stack (the hardware stack pointer stays
parked there, la_asm.h ccall), so both answers were wrong and the stack
never grew: RangeError at the first segment.  On e2k the active stack is
the central one when it has no parent (as shrink_stack decides), and the
overflow is checked with the stack pointer of the wasm frame.
---
 chromium/v8/src/wasm/wasm-external-refs.cc | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chromium/v8/src/wasm/wasm-external-refs.cc b/chromium/v8/src/wasm/wasm-external-refs.cc
index 582631e38e..6d4b2daee2 100644
--- a/chromium/v8/src/wasm/wasm-external-refs.cc
+++ b/chromium/v8/src/wasm/wasm-external-refs.cc
@@ -1442,13 +1442,29 @@ void switch_from_the_central_stack_for_js(Isolate* isolate) {
 // frame_size includes param slots area and extra frame slots above FP.
 Address grow_stack(Isolate* isolate, void* current_sp, size_t frame_size,
                    size_t gap, Address current_fp) {
+#if V8_TARGET_ARCH_E2K
+  // C code called from a secondary stack runs on the main stack on e2k (the
+  // hardware stack pointer stays there, see la_asm.h, ccall): the stack to
+  // grow is the active one, and the main stack is the one without a parent
+  // (as in shrink_stack).
+  if (isolate->isolate_data()->active_stack() == nullptr ||
+      isolate->isolate_data()->active_stack()->jmpbuf()->parent == nullptr) {
+#else
   if (isolate->IsOnCentralStack()) {
+#endif
     // Should not grow the central stack.
     return 0;
   }
   // Check if this is a real stack overflow.
+#if V8_TARGET_ARCH_E2K
+  // The stack pointer of C is not on the active stack (above): that of wasm is current_sp.
+  if (reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(current_sp) - gap <
+      reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(
+          isolate->isolate_data()->active_stack()->jslimit())) {
+#else
   StackLimitCheck check(isolate);
   if (check.WasmGrowableStackHasOverflowed(gap)) {
+#endif
     wasm::StackMemory* active_stack = isolate->isolate_data()->active_stack();
     DCHECK(active_stack->IsActive());
     // Grow by at least the new frame size plus the stack limit margin.
